    </header>
    <body>
        <segment id="1" parent="11" relname="span">Intuitiveness is a very important principle in interface design.</segment>
        <segment id="2" parent="1" relname="elaboration">It is important for users to be able to easily use an interface without becoming frustrated.</segment>
        <segment id="3" parent="4" relname="concession">Intuitive design is hard to measure</segment>
        <segment id="4" parent="12" relname="span">but we could look at using quantitative/ performance based measuremnts that can look at how long users take to accomplish partiicular tasks.</segment>
        <segment id="5" parent="6" relname="purpose">Also, we can collect feedback from users during tests of the interface</segment>
        <segment id="6" parent="14" relname="span">to see how well the interface flows and if there are any rough areas that could be re-worked.</segment>
        <segment id="7" parent="14" relname="elaboration">User feedback is probably the best tool to assess how intuitive a interface is.</segment>
        <segment id="8" parent="9" relname="background">This is one common msitakes many interface designers make;</segment>
        <segment id="9" parent="15" relname="span">not going back to see what users think about the design of the interface.</segment>
        <group id="10" type="span"/>
        <group id="11" type="span" parent="10" relname="span"/>
        <group id="12" type="span" parent="17" relname="span"/>
        <group id="13" type="span" parent="16" relname="span"/>
        <group id="14" type="span" parent="13" relname="span"/>
        <group id="15" type="span" parent="13" relname="elaboration"/>
        <group id="16" type="span" parent="12" relname="elaboration"/>
